# GitHub PAT for agency-os-github - ONLY needed in Cowork.
#
# IMPORTANT: A PAT is personal and applies per working copy. It belongs in a
# LOCAL, gitignored secrets file (.agency-os/secrets.env in the brain), NEVER in
# the committed/shared {context}/secrets.env - otherwise it ends up in all clones/the team.
# Make sure the file is gitignored (e.g. rule .agency-os/secrets.env).
#
# On a machine with an SSH key (Claude Code) the key is used and this entry is ignored.
# In Cowork the backup runs in an isolated sandbox without an SSH key and
# authenticates via token.
#
# Fine-grained PAT recommended: access only to the brain repo, permission
# "Contents: Read and write". That covers pull (incl. rebase) and push.
# A classic token with repo scope works too (then applies to all repos).
GITHUB_TOKEN=
